# The optional resilience series (docs/RESILIENCE.md): does an in-broker wasm
# deployment survive leadership moving, what does latency do while it
# happens, and how long until it is normal again? Maintenance mode and an
# explicit leadership transfer, each with graceful drain unset vs set.
#
#   scripts/autorun.sh check plans/resilience.plan
#   scripts/autorun.sh start plans/resilience.plan
#
# 3 brokers + clients + monitoring, ~$40/hr; ~1.5h of phases.
#
# Stateless relay latency during moves. For whether a STATEFUL guest's
# book survives the same moves (and broker kills), see book-durability.plan.

TOPOLOGY=single-az
DEPLOY_ARGS=()

# Four arms: {maintenance, transfer} x graceful drain {unset, 200ms}.
phase resilience-drain-ab 30 run resilience 'ACTIONS=maintenance transfer' DRAIN_AB=1
# Eight arms: the same, crossed with module residency {0, 8} - the series the
# published figures in docs/RESILIENCE.md come from.
phase resilience-residency 60 run resilience 'ACTIONS=maintenance transfer' DRAIN_AB=1 'RESIDENCY_LEVELS=0 8'
